WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:05.010
Tributes around the city are piling ever higher.

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:10.660
As grief sets in, New Zealanders are finding
ways to express their sorrow over a massacre

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:11.940
in their Muslim community.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:12.940
Police forensic work is continuing around
the mosques.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:13.940
But the bodies of all of the victims have
been removed from the crime scenes.

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:17.130
For now it's still a crime scene.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:22.180
But police are picking up flowers to take
closer to Al Noor mosque, where dozens of

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:28.860
people were slaughtered during their Friday
prayers.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:38.329
On the other side of the park, Christian groups
gathered to pray for their Muslim neighbors.

00:00:38.329 --> 00:00:43.530
One woman has brought an art project meant
to show the bond between all faiths.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:50.720
"So this is an artwork that I did for today
for St. Patrick's Day.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:01:03.030
I wanted to make something for the whole community
to acknowledge this sadness and sorrow and

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:11.600
that feeling of connection with the Muslim
community."

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.090
This man has found another way to show his
support.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:20.280
"I've had quite a few people come and have
coffees and hugs so it's been nice.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:27.150
I guess it's nice to see people just showing
up and showing their support and solidarity

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:31.799
which I think is what New Zealand is all about-
being open and welcoming and peaceful people."

00:01:31.799 --> 00:01:35.110
The support for the victims is overwhelming.

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:39.369
Most here are satisfied with the government's
response to the murders, but they want to

00:01:39.369 --> 00:01:42.360
know how the suspect slipped through the cracks.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:48.230
They say more needs to be done to address
racism- and to combat far-right radicalization

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:53.710
"Maybe we can't help the people who already
feel like that but we can at least stop the

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:58.850
younger ones from replicating this if we can."

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:03.500
The message here is clear: that hate has no
place in New Zealand.

